The only case of that I can think of is when you see a monster wield a
cursed weapon (which welds itself to the monster's hand); when you pick
this up later, you know it's cursed.

And, of course, if you put on any armor you'll know its enchantment (but
not before that).

Are you sure you didn't pick up your own previously discarded items?

> 2. I was surprised to see Asmodeus read a scroll of teleport and
> vanish. ... Are the named allowed
> to read teleport scrolls, and thus perhaps levelport, on their own
> level (which I thought were all no-teleport)? 

Anybody is allowed to read teleport scrolls on any no-teleport level. If
it's not cursed and you're not confused, nothing happens; if it's cursed
or you're confused or both, it level teleports you. There's nothing
against level teleporting off a no-teleport level.
 
